{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\PhotoEditor\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "private-api",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/Migration/RegisterMimeType.php:89 OC"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 use of the private API of the server in 1 file. Only OCP and NCU are public: what is below OC changes without notice between majors.",
        "  lib/Migration/RegisterMimeType.php:89 OC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boot-listener",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:123 injectFn()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "boot() registers a listener or takes a service from the container in 1 place. boot() runs once for every process of the server, so each of them is built on every request. registerEventListener() in register() builds a listener only when its event fires.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:123 injectFn()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/photo_editor/api/file/{fileId}  photo_editor.file.getfile  appinfo/routes.php:14 routes",
        "GET /index.php/apps/photo_editor/settings/admin  photo_editor.adminsettings.index  appinfo/routes.php:24 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 2 routes outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 23 files of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/photo_editor/api/file/{fileId}  photo_editor.file.getfile  appinfo/routes.php:14 routes",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/photo_editor/settings/admin  photo_editor.adminsettings.index  appinfo/routes.php:24 routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "vimeo/psalm, friendsofphp/php-cs-fixer, phpunit/phpunit are in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "config-without-lexicon",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Config/AppConfig.php:73 getAppValueString()",
        "lib/Config/AppConfig.php:95 setAppValueString()",
        "lib/Config/AppConfig.php:106 getAppValueString()",
        "lib/Config/AppConfig.php:127 setAppValueString()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "The app reads and writes its app config in 4 places and registers no config lexicon, which IRegistrationContext::registerConfigLexicon() takes since Nextcloud 31. A lexicon states the type, the default and the sensitivity of each key in one place.",
        "  lib/Config/AppConfig.php:73 getAppValueString()",
        "  lib/Config/AppConfig.php:95 setAppValueString()",
        "  lib/Config/AppConfig.php:106 getAppValueString()",
        "  lib/Config/AppConfig.php:127 setAppValueString()"
      ],
